[DC1-C — the completion corollary (REPORTING; Z is SUPPLIED data, D50: the form remains a choice)]
  [PASS] DC1-C d42b3's GRADIENT COMPLETION, re-derived and anchored to its OWN committed numbers (D1(ii)): Z(empty) = 1037/64, Z > 0 throughout, and Z constant on d42b3's canonical classes.  Under the completed kernel P_Z(e|h) = q Z(h+e)/Z(h) — which IS normalised per cut by the recursion — the commuting-square identity HOLDS on every commuting pair with both continuations inside Z's domain.  STATED HONESTLY: this is a property of a SUPPLIED completion, not of the generated law; its cost is d42b3's own (within-cut ratio deformation at 21 of 114 interior classes, the root included), and its domain here is parents of depth <= 2  (Z(empty) = 1037/64 (d42b3 anchor 1037/64); Z-class splits = 0; commuting pairs in Z's domain = 403; identity failures under P_Z = 0)

  THE GENERAL COROLLARY [PROOF — two lines, from two gated
  ingredients; printed, not gated, because it is algebra]:
    Let Z be ANY positive completion that factors through
    (depth, sigma) — i.e. Z(h) = Zhat(|h|, sigma(h)).  Then for
    every COMMUTING pair,
        P_Z(a|H) P_Z(b|Ha) = q(a|H) q(b|Ha) Z(Hab) / Z(H)
        P_Z(b|H) P_Z(a|Hb) = q(b|H) q(a|Hb) Z(Hba) / Z(H)
    (both telescope), and the two right-hand sides are EQUAL:
    the raw products agree by DC1(b) [gated above, 0
    exceptions], and Z(Hab) = Z(Hba) because |Hab| = |Hba| and
    sigma(Hab) = sigma(Hba) is the definition of the commuting
    class.  So the DC1 defect is annihilated by ANY completion
    of that shape.
    THE CORPUS ALREADY HAS ONE.  D49's root-free completion
    Zhat(h) = 2^(-|h|) . f(class(sigma(h))) (lambda = 2,
    f = (4,4,3,7,3,3)/3) has EXACTLY that shape and is
    normalised per cut at every depth at this scope (D49 +
    (H1)/(H2)).  So: the generated law's NORMALISED MENU KERNEL
    does not descend, and the SAME law read through the
    corpus's own selected completion does.  The price is
    named and unchanged: D50 — the stationary FORM of Z is a
    CHOICE, i.e. supplied, not derived.  That is why DC4 item 2
    stands as supplied and is now priced rather than moved.

