  DC1 — FAILS.  THE FAILURE IS THE DELIVERABLE (pin §2/§4).
  88632 of 665286 commuting pairs violate
  P(a|H)P(b|Ha) = P(b|H)P(a|Hb).  Its structure is COMPLETE:
    - the RAW products always agree (DC1(b)), so the
      generated law's unnormalised history weight IS
      order-independent on commuting pairs;
    - the entire defect is the NORMALISATION: exactly
      d = M(sigma(Hb))/M(sigma(Ha)), the coboundary of the
      per-state menu mass (DC1(c)) — a MASS-RATIO COCYCLE,
      the pin's pre-registered structural fallback, in its
      sharpest form;
    - the defect spectrum is exactly {'1': 576654, '4/5': 44316, '5/4': 44316};
    - it is a function of (sigma(H), class(a), class(b))
      alone under both key resolutions (DC1(d));
    - it VANISHES exactly on same-mass intermediates and
      occurs at every mass-mixed pair (DC1(e)) — the pin's
      lean was right, and nothing else fails.
  CONSEQUENCE, stated exactly and no wider: there is NO
  positive measure on refined record cylinders at this
  scope whose conditionals are the generated NORMALISED
  kernel — paper 29 Theorem 1's contrapositive, applied to
  a system that satisfies its three positivity hypotheses
  (DC3(4)) and its cylinder-identity hypothesis (DC1(f)).
  This does NOT contradict Theorem 1 (a theorem), and it is
  NOT an F1 hit: F1 asks for a MEASURE with unequal
  products; what is exhibited is a conditional system that
  is not induced by any such measure.  The generated law is
  ORDER-WEIGHTED at the normalised level, and any map from
  the action line's conditional-measure reading to it must
  carry order data or supply a completion (DC1-C).

  DC2 — RESTATEMENT, satisfied.  pi = sigma; fibre constancy
  is (H1); the 36-row kernel is printed.  NOT A NEW RESULT.
  DC3 — (1) SUBSTANTIVE, PASS; (2) reporting-only, trivially
